closest-possible
Same network, arithmetic and random draws (thresholds of the 13 neurons, then the synapse weights, in the reference's connection order); every sum is added in the order of the reference's synapse lists. The reference's Neuron/Synapse objects with index lists are flat f64 arrays (a different data shape, hence closest-possible). exp is the C library's, as Rust's f64::exp is. The answer is the sum of the four outputs; the benchmark harness hashes it as the reference's helper does. Stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback.
